(as amended) of the Town &amp; Country Planning Act 1990.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;
mso-fareast-language:EN-US&quot;&gt;Trees &amp;amp; Landscaping&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-language:
EN-US&quot;&gt; - Prior to the commencement of development, details of landscaping and
tree protection shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local
Planning Authority showing:&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;
mso-fareast-language:EN-US&quot;&gt;a) The location, species and approximate size of
all existing trees and shrubs on the site, clearly identifying those to be
retained and those to be removed, together with brief justification for any
proposed removal;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;
mso-fareast-language:EN-US&quot;&gt;b) Tree protection measures for retained trees and
adjacent street trees, including details of any protective measures during
construction.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;
mso-fareast-language:EN-US&quot;&gt;c) A soft landscaping scheme for the site,
including details of all proposed planting (species, size, number and
location), including replacement and additional tree planting where
appropriate.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;
mso-fareast-language:EN-US&quot;&gt;The development shall be carried out in accordance
with the approved details, and all planting shall be implemented in the first
planting season following completion of the development. Any trees or plants
which die, are removed or become seriously damaged or diseased within five
years of planting shall be replaced with specimens of similar size and species.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;









&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;
mso-fareast-language:EN-US&quot;&gt;Reason:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-language:EN-US&quot;&gt; To ensure the
protection of existing trees, including street trees, and to secure appropriate
landscaping and replacement planting in accordance with London Plan Policy G7
and Merton Local Plan Policy O15.4.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
